# Trading Platform

A real-time order execution, matching, position-keeping, and trade
surveillance platform built to exercise production-grade distributed
systems patterns end to end: event-driven microservices, idempotent
processing, database-per-service, container orchestration, CI/CD, and
an agentic AI compliance investigator.

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph Client
        UI[React Dashboard]
    end

    subgraph Services
        OG[Order Gateway]
        ME[Matching Engine]
        PS[Position Service]
        SS[Surveillance Service]
    end

    subgraph Infra
        K[(Kafka)]
        R[(Redis)]
        PG1[(Postgres - orderdb)]
        PG2[(Postgres - positiondb)]
        PG3[(Postgres - surveillancedb)]
        AN[Anthropic API]
    end

    UI -- REST + WebSocket --> OG
    OG -- order-events --> K
    K -- order-events --> ME
    K -- order-events --> OG
    ME -- trade-events --> K
    K -- trade-events --> PS
    K -- trade-events --> OG
    PS -- position-events --> K
    K -- position-events --> OG
    OG -- order-cancelled-events --> K
    K -- order-cancelled-events --> SS
    SS -- tool calls --> OG
    SS -- tool calls --> PS
    SS -- investigate --> AN

    OG --- PG1
    OG --- R
    PS --- PG2
    SS --- PG3
```

## Services

| Service | Responsibility | Tech |
|---|---|---|
| **Order Gateway** | Accepts orders via REST, idempotent placement, publishes order events, bridges Kafka → WebSocket for the live dashboard | Spring Boot, Kafka, Redis, Postgres, WebSocket/STOMP |
| **Matching Engine** | In-memory limit order book per symbol, price-time priority matching, produces trades | Spring Boot, Kafka (no HTTP surface by design) |
| **Position Service** | Event-sourced position/P&L tracking with weighted average cost, idempotent trade consumption, trade blotter history | Spring Boot, Kafka, Postgres |
| **Surveillance Service** | Rule-based spoofing detection, AI agent investigation with real tool-calling, compliance alert API | Spring Boot, Kafka, Postgres, Anthropic API |

## Why these design decisions (interview talking points)

- **Event-driven, not synchronous REST-to-REST** — services are decoupled;
  a slow/down Matching Engine never blocks order placement.
- **Idempotency at two layers** — client-order-ID uniqueness (DB
  constraint + Redis fast-path cache) on the way in, event-ID dedup
  table on the way out (Position Service, Surveillance Service) —
  Kafka's at-least-once delivery is handled correctly, not ignored.
- **Database-per-service** — Order Gateway, Position Service, and
  Surveillance Service each own an isolated Postgres instance; no
  service ever queries another's database directly.
- **Price-time priority matching** — a real limit order book (two
  priority queues, price + arrival-sequence ordering), not a toy CRUD
  simulation.
- **Weighted average cost + realized P&L** — correctly handles adds,
  partial closes, full closes, and long/short flips in one formula.
- **Two-stage AI surveillance** — cheap deterministic rules run on
  every event; the expensive LLM investigation (with real tool-calling
  against live services) only runs on the rare flagged case.
- **Kubernetes** — Deployments, Services, Secrets, PVCs, readiness vs.
  liveness vs. startup probes, and the deliberate simplifications made
  (single-replica Postgres/Kafka rather than StatefulSets) are all
  understood tradeoffs, not oversights.

## Running locally

**Docker Compose** (fastest path):
```bash
docker compose up --build
```

**Kubernetes (Minikube)**:
```bash
eval $(minikube docker-env)
# build all 4 service images with `docker build -t <service>:latest .`
kubectl apply -f k8s/
```

The React dashboard (`dashboard/`) needs a `.env` (see `.env.example`)
pointing at whichever backend you're running against, then:
```bash
cd dashboard && npm install && npm run dev
```

## Repository layout

```
trading-platform/
├── order-gateway/        # REST API, idempotency, WebSocket bridge
├── matching-engine/       # Order book + matching algorithm
├── position-service/      # Position/P&L tracking + trade blotter
├── surveillance-service/  # Rule-based detection + AI agent
├── dashboard/             # React live dashboard
├── k8s/                   # Kubernetes manifests
├── docker-compose.yml
└── .github/workflows/     # CI: test + build + push image per service
```